---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';
import kernels from '../../data/verified-kernels.json';
import models from '../../data/stateright-models.json';
import '../../styles/kernels.css';

type Kernel = (typeof kernels)[number];
type Model = (typeof models)[number] & {
  kafka?: string;
  outside?: string;
  pinned_states?: { config: string; count: number }[];
};

const kernelAreas = [...new Set(kernels.map((k: Kernel) => k.area))];
const modelAreas = [...new Set(models.map((m: Model) => m.area))];
const modelsByArea = (area: string) => (models as Model[]).filter((m) => m.area === area);
const pinnedTotal = (models as Model[]).reduce(
  (sum, m) => sum + (m.pinned_states ?? []).reduce((s, p) => s + p.count, 0),
  0,
);
const formatCount = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Verification Playground"
  description="Evaluate Krabka's Creusot-verified decision kernels in WebAssembly and browse every Stateright model with its bounds, properties, and pinned state counts."
  currentSlug="/docs/verification-playground"
>
  <div class="space-y-6 font-sans">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Verification Playground</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-sm max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
        Run the proved kernels in your browser, and read what each Stateright model checks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Krabka keeps its safety-critical decisions in <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-verified</code>,
        a crate of small pure functions whose contracts Creusot proves. Because those kernels do no I/O, the
        crate compiles to WebAssembly unchanged. The explorer below calls the same compiled bodies that the
        broker calls, so the answer you see is the answer the broker would give. Beside each result is the
        function's <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">requires</code> and
        <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">ensures</code> contract, quoted from the source.
      </p>
      <p>
        The kernels here are {kernels.length} of the crate's decision functions, chosen because their inputs fit
        a form. The <a href={getPath('/docs/broker/verification')} class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300 font-semibold">verification catalog</a>
        lists every proved kernel and every model.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Kernel explorer -->
    <h2 id="kernels" class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Creusot-verified kernel explorer</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 -mt-2">
      Areas: {kernelAreas.join(', ')}. Pick a kernel, edit its inputs, and the result updates as you type. An
      input that breaks a precondition is reported rather than evaluated, because the proof says nothing about
      inputs outside the contract.
    </p>

    <script type="application/json" id="krabka-kernel-specs" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(kernels)}></script>
    <div id="krabka-kernels" class="not-prose">
      <p class="kx-fallback">
        Loading the verified kernel explorer. This panel needs JavaScript and WebAssembly. If it does not
        appear, your browser may have them disabled.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Stateright gallery -->
    <h2 id="models" class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-4">Stateright model gallery</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Where correctness depends on a sequence of crashes, retries, and interleavings rather than on one
        decision, Krabka writes a Stateright model. The checker enumerates every reachable state within the
        model's bounds and prints a counterexample trace if a property fails. Each model's runner asserts its
        unique-state count against a pinned constant, so a search that silently shrinks fails the build.
      </p>
      <p>
        The models cannot run in this page. They live as test modules inside the broker and client crates,
        which depend on networking and file I/O that WebAssembly does not provide, and the checker itself
        uses threads. What this gallery gives you instead is the inventory: {models.length} model entry
        points, what production code each one drives, its bounds, its properties, and the
        {formatCount(pinnedTotal)} pinned unique states they cover between them. Every figure comes from
        the verification catalog, which pull request CI keeps in step with the models.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-8 not-prose">
      {modelAreas.map((area) => (
        <section>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white mb-3">{area}</h3>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">
            {modelsByArea(area).map((m) => (
              <article id={`model-${m.id}`} class="frosted-card rounded-2xl p-5 border border-white/10 flex flex-col gap-3">
                <div>
                  <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                    <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-white">{m.name}</h4>
                    <span class="rounded bg-white/5 border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 text-[10px] font-medium text-gray-400 whitespace-nowrap">{m.repo}</span>
                  </div>
                  <a
                    href={m.source_url}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="mt-1 inline-block font-mono text-[11px] text-krab-300 hover:text-krab-200 break-all"
                  >
                    {m.path}
                  </a>
                </div>

                <p class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">{m.summary}</p>

                {m.drives && m.drives.length > 0 && (
                  <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1">Drives</div>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
                      {m.drives.map((d) => (
                        <code class="rounded bg-black/40 border border-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-gray-200">{d}</code>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                )}

                {m.bounds && (
                  <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1">Bounds</div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">{m.bounds}</p>
                  </div>
                )}

                {m.properties && m.properties.length > 0 && (
                  <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1">Properties</div>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
                      {m.properties.map((p) => (
                        <code class="rounded bg-krab-500/10 border border-krab-500/30 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-krab-300">{p}</code>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                )}

                {m.pinned_states && m.pinned_states.length > 0 && (
                  <div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-400 mb-1">Pinned unique states</div>
                    <table class="w-full text-left text-[11px]">
                      <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5">
                        {m.pinned_states.map((p) => (
                          <tr>
                            <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono text-gray-300">{p.config}</td>
                            <td class="py-1 font-mono text-white text-right">{formatCount(p.count)}</td>
                          </tr>
                        ))}
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                  </div>
                )}

                {m.outside && (
                  <p class="text-[11px] text-gray-500 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/5 pt-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold text-gray-400">Outside the model:</span> {m.outside}
                  </p>
                )}
              </article>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">How the explorer works</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-gray-300">
        <li>The site build compiles <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">krabka-verified</code> at the pinned broker release into the same WebAssembly module as the consensus playground.</li>
        <li>The page serialises your inputs to JSON and hands them to one dispatcher function in the module.</li>
        <li>The dispatcher checks the kernel's <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">requires</code> clauses first. Inputs outside the contract come back as a precondition report and never reach the kernel.</li>
        <li>Inputs inside the contract run the proved body, and the result comes back as JSON for the page to render.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        The bindings live in <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">playground/src/kernels.rs</code> in this
        repository. They add no logic of their own: each arm parses a request, checks the preconditions the
        catalog lists for the caller, and calls the kernel.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Related Resources</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 not-prose pt-1">
        <a href={getPath('/docs/playground')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Consensus Playground →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Drive the deterministic KRaft engine itself: partitions, dropped and reordered messages, elections.</p>
        </a>
        <a href={getPath('/verification')} class="p-4 rounded-xl frosted-card border border-white/10 hover:border-krab-500/50 transition-colors block">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white">Correctness & Verification →</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-1">Safe Rust, Creusot proofs, Stateright models, and where the formal boundary ends.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>

<script src={getPath('/playground/kernels.js')} type="module" is:inline></script>
